1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:07,630
A storage class decides where a variable lives, its starting value, where it can be seen, and how long it lasts.

2
00:00:07,630 --> 00:00:10,312
Auto is the default for local variables.

3
00:00:10,312 --> 00:00:14,401
Extern variables are global, visible everywhere.

4
00:00:14,401 --> 00:00:16,223
Static ones keep their value.

5
00:00:16,223 --> 00:00:19,205
Register asks for a fast CPU register.

6
00:00:19,205 --> 00:00:25,755
And beware: an automatic variable you forget to initialise contains rubbish, not zero.

